@startuml 03k-deployment-cluster-integration-gap
!include ../_style.iuml
title sphinx-asr on the ivalice cluster: what exists today vs what the cluster docs assume

node "dalmasca (head)" as H {
  component "slurmctld" as CTL
  folder "/srv/ivalice/sphinx-asr\n(SPHINX_ROOT, planned)" as ROOT #FFFFFF
}
node "worker x5" as W {
  component "slurmd" as SD
}

component "sphinx.sh run_script()" as RS
component "SphinxTrain Queue layer\nCFG_QUEUE_TYPE" as Q
component "Queue::POSIX\n(templates default)" as QP
component "Queue::PBS (qsub)" as QPBS
component "Queue::Slurm\n(proposed, ~150 lines Perl,\ndocs/uml/04-slurm-integration)" as QS

RS --> Q
Q --> QP : today: forks CFG_NPART jobs\non ONE node
Q ..> QPBS : needs Torque qsub
Q ..> QS : not written
QS ..> CTL : sbatch ~--dependency=afterok
CTL --> SD
QP ..> H : all work on the node running "sphinx train"

note bottom of ROOT #FFE4E1
  Gaps between docs and code (as of the commits read):
  1. No NFS server/client packages or exports in the image.
  2. No stage 10-sphinx-asr and no 60-sphinx-asr.yml playbook;
     the image does not contain sphinx-asr, wheels, or bin/aarch64.
  3. sphinx.sh qsub path targets missing scripts/sphinx_job.sh.
  4. Templates set CFG_NPART = DEC_CFG_NPART = 1 and Queue::POSIX,
     so even on one CM4 only one of 4 cores is used until raised to 4.
  5. Experiment paths are written as absolute paths into
     sphinx_train.cfg at setup time, so setup must run under the
     same SPHINX_ROOT path every node will see.
end note
@enduml
